+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional due date (`yyyy-MM-dd`) with a computed `overdue` flag, settable
+via the JSON API, filterable with `GET /todos?overdue=`, and shown on the list page with a „nur
+überfällige“ toggle.
+
+**Architecture:** `TodoStore` owns date validation (throws `ValidationException`) and the overdue
+rule (via an injected `TimeProvider`). It returns `Todo` records with `Overdue` computed at read
+time to both the API and the Blazor page. `Program.cs` only adds the query parameter; the page only
+renders.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, ASP.NET Core minimal API, Blazor interactive server, xUnit,
+`WebApplicationFactory<Program>`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-14-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages (the test clock is a hand-written `TimeProvider` subclass).
+- Validation errors are `ValidationException`s thrown by `TodoStore`. The message for a bad date is
+  exactly `dueDate must be a date in the form YYYY-MM-DD`.
+- Dates are parsed with `DateOnly.TryParseExact(value, "yyyy-MM-dd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out _)`.
+- Overdue = `!Done && DueDate < today`, where today = `DateOnly.FromDateTime(time.GetUtcNow().UtcDateTime)`.
+  No date → never overdue.
+- JSON shape: `{"id":1,"title":"…","done":false,"dueDate":"2026-10-20","overdue":false}`, with
+  `"dueDate":null` when there is no date.
+- New UI elements get `data-testid`: `overdue-filter`, `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`. Labels: „nur
+  überfällige“ and „überfällig“. No styling, no sorting.
+- TDD: failing test first. Run everything with `dotnet test` from the repo root.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Clock passing midnight: a todo due today becomes overdue tomorrow without any write. Test
+  `OverdueFollowsTheClock` (Task 1).
+- Leap days: `2028-02-29` is valid, `2027-02-29` is rejected. Test `AcceptsLeapDaysOnlyInLeapYears` (Task 1).
+- Padded or non-ISO strings (`" 2026-10-20 "`, `"2026-10-20T00:00:00"`, `""`) are rejected, not
+  silently trimmed. Test `RejectsMalformedDueDates` (Task 1).
+- Marking an overdue todo done drops it from `overdue=true`. Test `DoneTodosLeaveTheOverdueFilter` (Task 2).
+- A PATCH with a non-string `dueDate` (`123`) is a 400, not a 500. Test `RejectsANonStringDueDate` (Task 3).
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Due date and overdue rule in the store (create + list)
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`
+- Create: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/FixedTimeProvider.cs`
+- Test: `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces:
